parameters.text:
=Extract the explicit personal name of the client/buyer from the text below. 
If no human name is found, return the word null.
Do not use markdown. Do not type ```json. Output ONLY a valid JSON object in this format: {"client_name": "Name"}

Text to analyze:
{{ $('Code in JavaScript').item.json.text }}

parameters.jsCode:
const rawResponse = $input.item.json.text || $input.item.json.output || "";

// ASCII code 96 is the backtick (`). This builds the string "```json|```" 
// at runtime so your editor's markdown parser cannot break the line.
const bt = String.fromCharCode(96, 96, 96);
const markdownSanitizer = new RegExp(bt + "json|" + bt, "gi");

const clean = rawResponse.replace(markdownSanitizer, "").trim();

let extractedName = null;
try {
    extractedName = JSON.parse(clean).client_name;
} catch(e) {}

const currentJob = $('Loop Over Items').item.json;

return {
    json: {
        ...currentJob,
        client_name: extractedName
    }
};

